Subject: [PATCH] Core: fix cached block offset when shrinking mraw allocations

The non-tail shrink path locates the free-block header using the released
size instead of the retained, aligned payload size. This can make the
cached block overlap live memory or extend beyond the original allocation.

Compute the header address before reusing new_size for the free-block
payload size. Extend the existing shrink test to check the cached payload
address as well as its size.

All 144 CTest tests pass with AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer.
Leak detection was disabled because LeakSanitizer cannot run under the
sandbox's tracing.

---
 source/lexbor/core/mraw.c | 2 +-
 test/lexbor/core/mraw.c   | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/source/lexbor/core/mraw.c b/source/lexbor/core/mraw.c
index c990405..2e629fb 100644
--- a/source/lexbor/core/mraw.c
+++ b/source/lexbor/core/mraw.c
@@ -352,8 +352,8 @@ lexbor_mraw_realloc(lexbor_mraw_t *mraw, void *data, size_t new_size)
         if (diff > lexbor_mraw_meta_size()) {
             memcpy(begin, &new_size, sizeof(size_t));
 
+            begin = &((uint8_t *) data)[new_size];
             new_size = diff - lexbor_mraw_meta_size();
-            begin = &((uint8_t *) data)[diff];
 
             lexbor_mraw_meta_set(begin, &new_size);
 
diff --git a/test/lexbor/core/mraw.c b/test/lexbor/core/mraw.c
index 03906d0..42a575a 100644
--- a/test/lexbor/core/mraw.c
+++ b/test/lexbor/core/mraw.c
@@ -438,6 +438,9 @@ TEST_BEGIN(mraw_realloc_n_less)
                  - (lexbor_mem_align(51) + lexbor_mraw_meta_size())
                  - lexbor_mraw_meta_size());
 
+    test_eq(mraw.cache->root->value,
+            one + lexbor_mem_align(51) + lexbor_mraw_meta_size());
+
     test_eq_size(mraw.mem->chunk_length, 1UL);
     test_eq_size(mraw.mem->chunk->size, 1024UL + lexbor_mraw_meta_size());
     test_eq_size(mraw.mem->chunk->length, 128UL + lexbor_mraw_meta_size()
